gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.purpose=A twin steam turbine that expands along its main shaft and converts steam into electricity.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.formula=Steady EU/t = §e40 × casing voltage × load × (2+extra rings) × singularity × steam × efficiency
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.baseline=LV steel array, ordinary steam, full load: the base ring counts as 2 groups, with a 150% efficiency cap and 20% steam savings.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.conditions=The two singularities are mutually exclusive. The chip requires all 4 extra rings.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.supply=Ordinary and superheated steam work from LV; dense or supercritical steam requires §bLuV §7or higher casings.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.rating=LV–UV casings determine the array voltage. Dynamo hatches need not match that tier.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.glass=All glass must have the same tier, at least the casing tier. Glass above UV is accepted.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.risk=Insufficient dynamo output capacity causes the array to explode.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.sample=At LuV voltage, running at full load.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.control=Right-click the controller with a screwdriver to cycle load settings.
gtsr.tooltip.mega_native.structure=Hold Left Shift to view the structure.
